.TH APKSYNC 8 "September 2026" "Saphira Linux" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
apksync \- repository synchronisation to publication mirrors
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B apksync
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B apksync
synchronises the local generation repositories outward to the
publication target with rsync (archive, compress, delayed updates).
In-flight
.I *.publishing-*
temporaries and the local
.I ownership.json
migration evidence are excluded and never leave the host.
.PP
Configuration comes from
.IR /etc/saphira/apksync.conf :
.I SAPHIRA_REPO_DIR
(the local source) and
.I SAPHIRA_SYNC_TARGET
(the mirror destination) are both required. Takes no arguments and
publishes nothing by itself; run it after
.BR sign-apk-repo (8),
then
.I apk update
on consumers.
.SH OPTIONS
This command takes no options.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/saphira/apksync.conf
Source and target configuration (both required).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Synchronised.
.TP
.B 1
Missing configuration or rsync failure.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.RS
sudo sign-apk-repo && sudo apksync && apk update
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR saphira (7),
.BR sign-apk-repo (8),
.BR installpkg (8),
.BR saphira-build (8)
